From 71df49b15d94160d8ca8018a4d2a4332e2498b1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:17:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Freeciv45 "what next" button above the minimap: research,
 unit orders, city production, then End turn

With gui_qt_freeciv45_edges on, a 224 x 40 button sits right-aligned with
the minimap, 8 px above it, and follows it when it moves, changes size or
hides (so it hides with the minimap while the city overlay is open, and
with the map while a report tab is current). It says what the turn needs
next, in decision 10's order, and a click does it:

- "Choose research" while nothing is being researched: opens the research
  report.
- "Unit needs orders" while an own unit is idle with moves left, no orders,
  not done and not automated (the units the focus cycles through, waiting
  ones included): the next one, as W does, or the first such unit when the
  focus unit has its orders.
- "City needs production" for an own city that finished something at this
  turn's start or was founded this turn and has nothing queued: opens it.
  The city's data decides (city_built_last_turn, not a founding stamp, and
  an empty worklist), since the worklist and production-changed events go
  to no message window by default. A city counts as seen for the rest of
  the turn once it is opened from here or shown in the overlay.
- "End turn" when nothing blocks, greyed out and highlighted as the
  sidebar's Turn Done is (side_disable_endturn, side_blink_endturn).

"1 of N" shows on the right when more than one thing waits; the tooltip says
what a click does. The button refreshes twice a second. Shift+Return still
ends the turn, and the top strip's End turn stays. Themed in the
NightStalker and System resource.qss; the labels carry the button's step,
since a pseudo-state of an ancestor does not reach a child in a style sheet.

panels.md section 8.3, issue 144.
